# (BERLIN, the Lead's FORGET: the user's design) in PERFORM the top key (G5, w15: key 26), set apart from the moves by
# the dark keys between, is lit steadily (not blinking: white 6 blinks, the solos blink), dark while held; a press:
# the Lead forgets its ideas and its theme ("LEAD FORGOTTEN", a card), nothing else changes. Out of PERFORM the key
# plays the Lead again
wait 500
turn PRESET 4
wait 300
expect piece 4
listen
tap SEL
wait 300
expect view 17
said PERFORM ON
expect litkey26 1
wait 250
expect litkey26 1
wait 250
expect litkey26 1
key w15 down
wait 100
said LEAD FORGOTTEN
expect litkey26 0
expect card 1
wait 400
expect litkey26 0
key w15 up
wait 100
expect litkey26 1
expect mutes 0
expect view 17
tap ENV
wait 300
expect view 1
said PERFORM OFF
key w15 down
wait 100
said_none FORGOTTEN
key w15 up
wait 300
